<title>PHILIPPINES: Petron says output stable despite blast.</title>
<headline>Petron says output stable despite blast.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petron Corp, the Philippines' biggest oil refiner, said on Monday an explosion at its refinery just north of Manila would have only a minimal effect on production.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still running at maximum 155,000 barrels of oil per day. While there will be a slight reduction in LPG, gasoline, and diesel production, this will not affect our capability to supply these products,&quot; a company source told Reuters when asked about the accident last Friday.</p>
</text>
